<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Antanas Smetona</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1874">1874</a>–<a href="/years/1944">1944</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Antanas Smetona was the first President of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lithuania">Lithuania</a>, from 1919 to 1920, and returned to power after the military coup of December 1926. He ruled as an authoritarian leader of the Nationalist Union until the Soviet ultimatum of June 1940, when he fled abroad. He died in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> in 1944.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/antanas-smetona.jpg" alt="Antanas Smetona" width="320" height="490" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Owned by the National Museum of Lithuania · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Antanas_Smetona_2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
